in common written and spoken situations. "}]}, {"type": "background_image", "content": "engenn5le07ob04re1img01.png"}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Swallowed Syllables"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "Non-stressed words and syllables are often \"swallowed\" in English."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Key words like nouns, pronouns, verbs or adjectives are stressed and other words like articles and  prepositions are shortened and weakened (\u201cswallowed\u201d). Syllables in words can also be \u201cswallowed\u201d."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Two or three swallowed words can  take up the same amount of time as one stressed syllables before or after it."}, {"type": "text", "content": " For example: "}, {"type": "text", "content": "<span class=\"italic\">I like walking in the park, </span>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "The syllables <span class=\"italic\">I / like / wal / park,</span> are stressed.<br> The 3 syllables <span class=\"italic\">kin / in / the,</span> are said much faster and blend together."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Remember:"}, {"type": "text", "content": "Focus on pronouncing stressed words well, non-stressed words are weaker and swallowed. <br> Focus on the stressed words in each sentence."}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "These are words you use when talking about relationships."}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Answering Simple Questions at Work"}, {"type": "describer", "content": " "}, {"type": "text", "content": "You are often asked simple questions at work like:"}, {"type": "table", "content": "{\"rows\":8,\"columns\":2,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" Question \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Possible Answer Example\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" What are you working on?\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"